# PHASE 2 — VISUAL IDENTITY: NEO-BRUTALISM, REIMAGINED FOR INDUSTRIAL AI

Create a distinctive visual identity combining expressive neo-brutalism with premium enterprise software design.

The website should feel bold, modern, tactile, intelligent, technical, and trustworthy. It must not look like a generic admin template, a conventional cybersecurity dashboard, or a collection of unrelated cards.

## Design principles

1. Bold typography and strong editorial hierarchy.
2. High-contrast outlines and confident geometry.
3. Clean modular layouts with intentional spacing.
4. Hard offset shadows used as a deliberate design feature.
5. Restrained gradients that provide depth and personality.
6. Vivid accent colors reserved for actions, findings, and focused elements.
7. Clear separation between operational information and advanced technical details.
8. Consistent visual language throughout the application.

Use neo-brutalism purposefully. Do not make every element loud, colorful, outlined, or heavily shadowed. The application is used to investigate potentially serious safety incidents, so clarity and credibility must take priority over decoration.

Avoid excessive glassmorphism, blurred translucent cards, glowing borders on every component, giant empty hero areas, overuse of gradients, and unnecessary animation.

## Suggested color system

Use this as the initial design-token proposal. Adjust contrast where necessary and apply the same semantic tokens across all components.

